Blinkit Retail Analytics is an end-to-end data analytics project developed using Python, Pandas, NumPy, Streamlit, Matplotlib, and Seaborn. The project focuses on generating synthetic retail data, cleaning and preprocessing datasets, handling missing values and duplicate records, and performing Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) to understand sales performance. It includes an interactive Streamlit dashboard with key performance indicators (KPIs), 14 visualization options, and filters for item type, outlet type, location tier, and fat content. The dashboard also provides data quality reports, business insights, descriptive statistics, and CSV download functionality for further analysis. This project demonstrates practical skills in Python programming, data cleaning, feature engineering, data visualization, and interactive dashboard development. It is designed to help understand retail sales trends and support data-driven business decisions using synthetic data, not official Blinkit data.